---
import SabFooter from '../components/sab/SabFooter.astro';
import SabFonts from '../components/sab/SabFonts.astro';
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
import SabHeader from '../components/sab/SabHeader.astro';
import { webPageJson } from '../lib/ld';

// Same rule as the privacy page: this date is the only thing telling a reader
// whether the document still matches the site. Bump it when the terms change.
const LAST_UPDATED = 'September 2, 2026';

const title = 'Terms of Use | ScholarAB';
const description = 'How to use ScholarAB, what the listings are and are not, and the limits of what a free student-built directory can promise.';
const ldJson = webPageJson({ name: 'Terms of Use', description, path: '/terms/' });
---

<Layout
  title={title}
  description={description}
  ogTitle={title}
  ogDescription={description}
  ogUrl="https://www.scholarab.ca/terms/"
>
  <script is:inline type="application/ld+json" set:html={JSON.stringify(ldJson)} slot="head" />
  <SabFonts italic slot="head" />

  <div class="sabp-header" slot="header">
    <SabHeader currentPath="/terms" />
  </div>

  <div id="sab-terms" class="sabp" style="display:flex;flex-direction:column;min-height:100%;">
    <div class="sabtm-body" style="flex:1;">
      <div class="sab-kicker">TERMS</div>
      <h1 class="sabtm-h1">Free to use,<br /><span class="sabtm-h1-accent">worth double-checking.</span></h1>
      <p class="sabtm-lede">
        ScholarAB is a free directory of Alberta scholarships and research programs, built and
        maintained by one high school student. There is no account to create and nothing to pay.
        These terms exist to be honest about what that means. Mostly, that a deadline listed here
        is a copy of someone else's deadline, and the provider's own page always wins.
      </p>
      <p class="sabtm-updated">Last updated {LAST_UPDATED}</p>

      <h2 class="sabtm-h2">Always confirm with the provider</h2>
      <p class="sabtm-p">
        Every listing is written from the provider's own page rather than scraped, and dated
        deadlines open and close on their own each day. Nothing here is continuously monitored,
        though: deadlines move, awards get discontinued, eligibility rules change quietly, and a
        listing can be wrong or out of date without anything on this site saying so.
      </p>
      <p class="sabtm-p">
        <strong>Before you apply, open the provider's own page and confirm the deadline, the amount,
        and whether you're eligible.</strong> Every listing links to it. Treat what you read here as a
        starting point for finding awards, never as the authoritative version of one.
      </p>

      <h2 class="sabtm-h2">No affiliation</h2>
      <p class="sabtm-p">
        ScholarAB is not affiliated with, endorsed by, or sponsored by any of the scholarship
        providers, universities, foundations, school divisions, or government programs it lists. We
        don't administer any award, don't receive or forward applications, don't sit on any selection
        committee, and have no say in who wins anything. Names and trademarks belonging to those
        organizations are used only to identify what a listing refers to.
      </p>

      <h2 class="sabtm-h2">The match quiz is a filter, not a ruling</h2>
      <p class="sabtm-p">
        The match tool narrows the directory using the eligibility rules recorded for each listing. It
        can be wrong in both directions, either hiding something you'd have qualified for, or showing
        something you wouldn't. Your answers never leave your browser, which also means we can't
        check them for you. If an award looks close, apply anyway and let the provider decide.
      </p>

      <h2 class="sabtm-h2">What we can't promise</h2>
      <p class="sabtm-p">
        ScholarAB is provided as-is, with no warranty of any kind. We can't promise the site will be
        available, that the information on it is complete, current, or accurate, or that using it will
        get you a scholarship. To the fullest extent the law allows, ScholarAB and its maintainer
        aren't liable for any loss that comes from using the site, including a missed deadline, a
        deadline listed wrong, an award that turns out not to exist, or a rejected application.
      </p>
      <p class="sabtm-p">
        This isn't an attempt to dodge responsibility for the work: mistakes get fixed quickly, and
        <!--email_off--><a href="mailto:contact.scholarab@gmail.com">telling us about one</a><!--/email_off--> is genuinely welcome. It is
        an acknowledgement that a free directory maintained by one person cannot carry the risk of
        your application, and that the provider's page is the record that counts.
      </p>

      <h2 class="sabtm-h2">Using the site</h2>
      <ul class="sabtm-list">
        <li>Browse, search, save, share, print, and hand the whole thing to your students. That's what it's for.</li>
        <li>Don't sign anyone else up for deadline reminders. Every sign-up is confirmed by email for exactly this reason.</li>
        <li>Don't hammer the site with automated requests, or try to break, overload, or get into parts of it that aren't public.</li>
        <li>Don't republish the listings as your own. See the licenses below for what reuse is allowed.</li>
      </ul>

      <h2 class="sabtm-h2">Reusing the code and the data</h2>
      <p class="sabtm-p">
        The site's source code is licensed under the GNU AGPL-3.0. The scholarship and program
        database is licensed separately under Creative Commons Attribution-ShareAlike 4.0. You may
        reuse it, including commercially, if you credit ScholarAB with a link and release your version
        under the same terms. Individual facts, like a deadline or a dollar amount, belong to nobody;
        what's licensed is the written descriptions and the selection and arrangement of the database.
        The name <strong>ScholarAB</strong> and the logo are not covered by either license.
      </p>
      <p class="sabtm-p">
        Full text: <a href="https://github.com/scholarab/scholarab/blob/main/LICENSE">LICENSE</a>,
        <a href="https://github.com/scholarab/scholarab/blob/main/DATA-LICENSE.md">DATA-LICENSE</a>,
        <a href="https://github.com/scholarab/scholarab/blob/main/TRADEMARK.md">TRADEMARK</a>.
      </p>

      <h2 class="sabtm-h2">Privacy</h2>
      <p class="sabtm-p">
        What the site collects, why, how long it's kept, and how to delete it are all set out on the
        <a href="/privacy/">privacy policy</a>. The short version: you can use the entire site without
        giving us anything, and the only personal information we ever hold is an email address you
        asked us to remind you at.
      </p>

      <h2 class="sabtm-h2">Changes, and which law applies</h2>
      <p class="sabtm-p">
        These terms can change; the date at the top moves when they do, and every version is in the
        site's public source history. They're governed by the laws of Alberta and of Canada.
      </p>

      <h2 class="sabtm-h2">If you run one of these programs</h2>
      <p class="sabtm-p">
        If you administer an award or program listed here and something about the listing is wrong,
        out of date, or you'd rather not be listed at all, email
        <!--email_off--><a href="mailto:contact.scholarab@gmail.com">contact.scholarab@gmail.com</a><!--/email_off--> and say so. A
        correction gets made as soon as it's read, and a request to be removed is honoured without
        argument, no explanation needed, and nothing has to be escalated to get it done. The same
        goes for anything you believe infringes your copyright: tell us what and where, and it comes
        down while we sort it out.
      </p>

      <h2 class="sabtm-h2">Changes to these terms</h2>
      <p class="sabtm-p">
        These terms can change. When they do, the date at the top of this page moves, and every
        earlier version stays in the site's public source history so you can see what changed.
        Continuing to use the site after a change means the new version applies.
      </p>

      <h2 class="sabtm-h2">Governing law</h2>
      <p class="sabtm-p">
        These terms are governed by the laws of the Province of Alberta and the federal laws of
        Canada that apply in it, and the courts of Alberta are where any dispute about them belongs.
        Nothing here takes away consumer rights that Alberta or Canadian law gives you and does not
        let you sign away. If a court finds any part of these terms unenforceable, that part is
        severed and the rest stays in force.
      </p>

      <h2 class="sabtm-h2">Contact</h2>
      <p class="sabtm-p">
        ScholarAB · Medicine Hat, Alberta, Canada<br />
        <!--email_off--><a href="mailto:contact.scholarab@gmail.com">contact.scholarab@gmail.com</a><!--/email_off-->
      </p>
    </div>
    <SabFooter />
  </div>
</Layout>

<style>
  .sabtm-body { padding: 72px 48px 110px; width: 100%; max-width: var(--sab-measure); margin: 0 auto; box-sizing: border-box; }

  .sabtm-h1 {
    font-family: 'Instrument Serif', Georgia, serif; font-weight: 400;
    font-size: clamp(40px, 6vw, 76px); line-height: 1.02; letter-spacing: -0.02em;
    color: #141915; margin: 12px 0 24px;
  }
  .sabtm-h1-accent { color: #0A6B4D; font-style: italic; }

  .sabtm-lede { font-size: 19px; line-height: 1.65; color: #3A403B; max-width: 62ch; margin: 0 0 12px; }
  .sabtm-updated {
    font-family: 'IBM Plex Mono', monospace; font-size: 12px; letter-spacing: 0.06em;
    text-transform: uppercase; color: #8A8F8B; margin: 0 0 56px;
  }

  .sabtm-h2 {
    font-family: 'Instrument Serif', Georgia, serif; font-weight: 400;
    font-size: clamp(26px, 3vw, 34px); letter-spacing: -0.01em; color: #141915;
    margin: 56px 0 20px; padding-top: 24px; border-top: 1px solid #E4E0D5;
  }

  .sabtm-p { font-size: 16px; line-height: 1.7; color: #3A403B; max-width: 68ch; margin: 0 0 18px; }
  .sabtm-p a, .sabtm-list a { color: #0A6B4D; }

  .sabtm-list { margin: 0; padding-left: 20px; max-width: 68ch; }
  .sabtm-list li { font-size: 16px; line-height: 1.7; color: #3A403B; margin-bottom: 12px; }

  @media (max-width: 760px) {
    .sabtm-body { padding: 48px 20px 80px; }
  }
</style>
